WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.210
Viserys Targaryen: When he looked east, he
saw the past: old, tired, dead.

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:15.309
But when he looked west, he saw the future:
gold in the ground, gold in the fields, and

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:18.750
no dragons in the sky but his.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:24.880
He and his sisters, Rhaenys and Visenya, flew
over the great continent, ostensibly visitors

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.590
to a strange land.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:33.059
But when Aegon returned, he ordered construction
of a massive table carved in the shape of

00:00:33.059 --> 00:00:37.539
Westeros, with all the notable rivers and
mountains that they had seen.

00:00:37.539 --> 00:00:46.200
A personal map of the Seven Kingdoms, then
ruled by seven squabbling families.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:53.420
House Durrandon held the Stormlands from their
seat at Storm's End, due south of Dragonstone.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.820
House Hoare of the Iron Islands had also conquered
and enslaved the Riverlands, and ruled them

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:04.770
from Harrenhal, a monstrous castle rising
on the shore of the Gods Eye.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:10.790
House Stark held the frozen wasteland of the
North, the oldest, largest, and emptiest of

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:11.790
the kingdoms.

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:17.930
House Lannister held the Westerlands, the
wealthiest kingdom thanks to their gold mines.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:23.430
House Gardener held the Reach, the second
wealthiest kingdom thanks to their crops.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:27.320
House Arryn held the Vale, or rather the Vale
held them.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:32.640
The mountains were impassable except through
the Bloody Gate, which had never been taken.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:38.910
House Martell held the deserts of Dorne, probably
because no one else wanted them.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:44.610
Together, the Seven Kingdoms made Westeros,
a realm that wasn't yet a realm, ruled by

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:49.320
great families who didn't know what greatness
was.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.480
Aegon would teach them.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:57.420
Varys: Though House Durrandon titled themselves
"Storm Kings," they were little more than

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:58.420
gusts.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:03.740
Their kingdom in the Stormlands had been doddering
to its end for the past few centuries, helped

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:05.290
along by other houses.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:11.039
Most of all by House Hoare, who were nearly
finished with a monstrous castle at Harrenhal,

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:15.549
too large and too costly a seat to rule only
the Riverlands.

00:02:15.549 --> 00:02:19.780
King Argilac knew where the Ironborn would
soon turn.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:23.709
You'd think a king who wanted to keep his
crown would be wary of a man with fire-breathing

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:29.159
monsters, but King ArgilacDurrandon wasn't
called "the Arrogant" for nothing.

00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:35.239
Determined to arrest decline, he sent an envoy
to Dragonstone to enlist Aegon Targaryen and

00:02:35.239 --> 00:02:37.439
his dragons against his enemies.

00:02:37.439 --> 00:02:43.040
In exchange, Argilac offered lands he didn't
have, and a wife Aegon didn't need.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:48.450
For as the Valyrians did, Aegon had wed his
elder sister Visenya.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:53.609
Then as the Valyrians didn't, he took the
younger Rhaenys as well.

00:02:53.609 --> 00:02:56.400
Two sisters, two wives.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.319
Perhaps that's why he was so keen to get off
Dragonstone.

00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:02.269
Aegon countered Argilac with courtesy.

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:08.290
He sent his own envoy requesting that Princess
Durrandon's hand be given instead to Aegon's

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:13.349
closest friend and rumored half-brother, Orys
Baratheon.

00:03:13.349 --> 00:03:18.450
Argilac answered with a box and a note: "These
are the only hands your bastard shall have

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:19.529
of me."

00:03:19.529 --> 00:03:24.139
Inside the box were the hands of Aegon's envoy.

00:03:24.139 --> 00:03:27.689
How long had Aegon been waiting for such a
pretext?

00:03:27.689 --> 00:03:33.779
As his army prepared to sail, ravens flew
to every great lord of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:39.909
All bore the same message: From this day forth,
there would be but one king in Westeros.

00:03:39.909 --> 00:03:45.310
Those who bent the knee to Aegon of House
Targaryen would keep their lands and titles.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:50.329
Those who took up arms against him would be
thrown down, humbled and destroyed.

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:52.939
Poor old Argilac.

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:56.069
He couldn't even match Aegon in arrogance.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:04:00.939
Aegon landed at the mouth of the Blackwater
River and raised a primitive Aegonfort in

00:04:00.939 --> 00:04:05.799
the disputed lands between Harren's and Argilac's
kingdom so that neither could decide whose

00:04:05.799 --> 00:04:07.409
problem he was.

00:04:07.409 --> 00:04:13.459
Adopting the customs of the Seven Kingdoms,
Aegon unfurled his own banner with a red three-headed

00:04:13.459 --> 00:04:16.759
dragon breathing fire upon a black field.

00:04:16.759 --> 00:04:22.620
Visenya crowned him with a ruby-studded circlet
of Valyrian steel while Rhaenys hailed him

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:27.300
as the first high king the continent had seen
since the Dawn Age.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:32.490
As his lords and the gathered locals cheered
him, Aegon named his loyal friends to a small

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:38.729
council led by Orys Baratheon, whom he called
"my strong right hand."

00:04:38.729 --> 00:04:43.740
The title stuck, and a bastard became the
first Hand of the King.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:49.800
But for now, Aegon's kingdom contained only
a rocky island and a handful of fields.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:54.760
The other kings had large armies, ships, castles,
and thousands of years of rule.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.169
But Aegon had dragons.

00:04:57.169 --> 00:05:02.139
He had chosen for the words of his house,
"Fire and Blood."

00:05:02.139 --> 00:05:07.270
Before he was done, the rivers, fields, and
skies would turn red.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:14.450
Euron Greyjoy: Harren of House Hoare inherited
a kingdom that stretched from the Iron Islands

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:16.060
to the Trident.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:21.080
Too great a kingdom to rule from a castle
as shit as Pyke.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:27.479
For forty years, his ironborn plundered the
Riverlands for stone, timber, and slaves to

00:05:27.479 --> 00:05:29.560
build a seat worthy of him.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:37.560
Legend has it that masons laid the final stone
in Harrenhal on the very day that Aegon landed

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.560
in Westeros.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:41.640
Could've been a divine omen.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:47.940
Could've been the masons wanted to go off
before the dragons got there.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:50.030
They weren't the only ones.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:55.970
At Aegon's approach, Harren'sriverlords revolted,
led by House Tully.

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:59.130
I doubt Harren noticed.

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:02.790
Harrenhal could repel an army of a million
men.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:07.680
No ladder could summit its walls, and ram
could shatter them.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.550
The castle was as impregnable as an old maid's...

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:17.990
Harren shut his gates around himself, his
sons and his ironborn, and waited for Aegon's

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:21.539
army to drain back into the muck.

00:06:21.539 --> 00:06:26.550
When Aegon finally saw the monstrous castle,
he asked for parley.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.120
Harren granted it.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:33.240
Valyria had been the greatest empire the world
had ever seen.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:37.120
Harren wanted to piss on its ashes.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:43.229
Viserys Targaryen: (as Aegon) "Yield now,
and you may remain Lord of the Iron Islands.

00:06:43.229 --> 00:06:47.930
Yield now, and your sons will live to rule
after you.

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:51.240
You see my army outside your walls.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.770
You see my dragons."

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:57.789
Euron: (as Harren) "What is outside my walls
is of no concern.

00:06:57.789 --> 00:06:59.639
Those walls are strong and thick."

00:06:59.639 --> 00:07:02.580
Viserys: (as Aegon) "Dragons fly."

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:06.090
Euron: (as Harren) "But stone doesn't burn."

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:11.250
Viserys: (as Aegon) "When the sun sets, your
line shall end."

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:15.699
Euron: Harren spat and returned to his castle.

00:07:15.699 --> 00:07:20.780
Once inside, he promised lands, riches, and
Tully's daughters to whoever could bring down

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:23.219
Aegon or his dragon.

00:07:23.219 --> 00:07:30.099
As the sun sank below the horizon, all Harren's
men patrolled the battlements, hearing wings

00:07:30.099 --> 00:07:33.080
in every gust of wind.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:38.250
But the moon rose and sank, and no dragon
appeared.

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:43.580
Viserys: While the ironborn were ringing the
battlements, Aegon drove his dragon Balerion

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:48.110
higher and higher in the night sky, so that
even the great castle of Harrenhallooked like

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:49.699
an anthill below them.

00:07:49.699 --> 00:07:55.220
Then they plunged straight into the castle,
well inside the guarded walls.

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:59.350
The five towers of Harrenhal reached towards
Aegon like a hand.

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:03.169
Balerion opened his mouth and bathed all the
fingers in flame.

00:08:03.169 --> 00:08:06.210
Euron: Harren was right.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:12.749
Stone doesn't burn, but men do, even when
they're ironborn.

00:08:12.749 --> 00:08:19.750
The dragon blasted my ancestors into ash that
choked the survivors when they screamed.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:23.340
Harren's soldiers leapt from the battlements
and died.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:27.629
They huddled against the walls and died.

00:08:27.629 --> 00:08:30.360
They fled across the yard and died.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:34.380
Harren and his sons took shelter inside the
castle.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:43.990
The stone didn't burn, but as Balerion blasted
it with fire, it glowed white-hot.

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:51.389
The world's greatest castle became the world's
greatest oven, baking the last of House Hoare

00:08:51.389 --> 00:08:52.570
within it.

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:58.450
Viserys: Outside the castle walls, the towers
of Harrenhal glowed red against the night

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:03.889
and began to twist and melt like five huge
candles, with liquid stone trickling down

00:09:03.889 --> 00:09:06.630
their sides like wax.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:10.550
The next morning, Aegon forged a new Riverlands.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:15.390
He named the rebel Edmyn Tully as his Lord
Paramount of the Trident and had the other

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:18.500
riverlords swear him fealty as their new liege.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:23.079
For centuries, House Hoare had terrorized
the Riverlands.

00:09:23.079 --> 00:09:29.149
Under House Tully, the Riverlands would, at
last, return to peace and prosperity.

00:09:29.149 --> 00:09:34.490
After the castle cooled enough to allow men
inside, Aegon ventured into the ruin he had

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:35.970
made of Harrenhal.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:42.250
He saw the ashen bodies, the scorched stone,
and the mangled and melted swords of his former

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:43.480
enemies.

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:50.420
To his men's confusion, he ordered these useless
swords collected and sent to his Aegonfort.

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:57.980
Varys: While Aegon marched on Harrenhal after
his coronation, Orys Baratheon had taken most

00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:02.769
of his forces, and his queen Rhaenys with
her dragon, south to deal with the excuse

00:10:02.769 --> 00:10:08.160
for the invasion: Argilac the Arrogant, King
of the Stormlands.

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:13.149
Argilac had his seat at Storm's End, a castle
considered the most impregnable in Westeros

00:10:13.149 --> 00:10:15.070
after Harrenhal.

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:19.120
Argilac may have been arrogant, but he wasn't
stupid or a coward.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:24.290
His lords advised him to shut his gates and
wait out the siege, but he'd heard what had

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:30.149
happened at Harrenhal and refused to die a
suckling pig cooked in his own castle.

00:10:30.149 --> 00:10:35.630
He would meet victory or defeat the same way,
with sword in hand.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:40.370
He called his banners and marched to meet
Orys Baratheon in the field.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:46.810
Thanks to Rhaenys' dragon, Meraxes, Orys knew
Argilac was coming, how many men he had, and

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.660
how fast he marched.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:54.440
So Orys simply seized the high ground and
dug in on the hills to wait for Argilac.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:58.700
As the two armies approached, the wind rose
to meet them, and the rain poured from the

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:04.420
sky, a gale which would give the battle its
name: the Last Storm.

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:09.920
King Argilac's lords urged him to wait for
the weather to die down, but the Storm King

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:16.050
saw that the rain was blowing into the faces
of the Baratheon men on their hills and Argilac

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:21.959
outnumbered the Baratheon host two to one,
with four times as many knights and heavy

00:11:21.959 --> 00:11:24.130
horse.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.250
Argilac attacked.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:31.740
Three times Argilac led his knights against
the Baratheon line, but the hills were steep,

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:34.820
and the rain had beat the earth mud.

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:39.320
The warhorses foundered and slipped, and the
chargers collapsed.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:44.139
The battle seemed lost until Argilac ordered
the spearmen up the hill.

00:11:44.139 --> 00:11:48.640
Blinded by the rain, the Baratheons didn't
see them until it was too late.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:56.750
One hill fell, then another and another until
only one remained in the Baratheon center.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:12:02.889
If Argilac could break through there, he could
split the invading army and flank both halves.

00:12:02.889 --> 00:12:10.800
Argilac and his men charged, and the Baratheon
line broke, revealing Queen Rhaenys and Meraxes.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:15.260
Argilac's vanguard burst into flame, and his
men panicked.

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:20.720
The victory charge fell into chaos, and Argilac
himself was thrown from his horse.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.759
But he didn't yield.

00:12:22.759 --> 00:12:28.190
When Orys Baratheon arrived, he found the
old king holding off half-a-dozen men, another

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:31.070
half-dozen dead at his feet.

00:12:31.070 --> 00:12:36.220
Orys dismounted to meet the king on equal
footing and offered Argilac one final chance

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:38.009
to yield.

00:12:38.009 --> 00:12:40.490
Argilac cursed him instead.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:45.660
As the storm raged around them, the grizzled
old warrior and the bearded upstart fought

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.810
for life and kingdom.

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:51.940
In the end, Argilac got his wish.

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:55.209
He died, sword in hand.

00:12:55.209 --> 00:13:01.649
As word of Argilac's death spread, his lords
and knights threw down their swords and fled.

00:13:01.649 --> 00:13:06.790
Orys and his vanguard rode to Storm's End
to claim Argilac's castle for Aegon, only

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:09.709
to find the gates barred and the walls manned.

00:13:09.709 --> 00:13:15.870
Argilac's daughter had assumed his crown,
and the new Storm Queen was as fond of yielding

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.769
as her father.

00:13:17.769 --> 00:13:23.009
She declared that Orys would win only bones,
blood, and ashes here.

00:13:23.009 --> 00:13:29.199
But her men were weaker than her, and that
night Orys found Argilac's daughter delivered,

00:13:29.199 --> 00:13:32.720
gagged, chained, and naked to his camp.

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:35.720
Argilac had refused to give Orys her hand.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:38.529
Now, Orys could have any part of her he wished.

00:13:38.529 --> 00:13:45.020
But Orys unchained the girl, wrapped his cloak
around her, and poured her a glass of wine.

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:49.750
He told her he would take the arms, banner,
and words of House Durrandon to honor her

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:52.600
father's courage in the Last Storm.

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:56.490
Conveniently, Orys had none of his own to
discard first.

00:13:56.490 --> 00:14:02.240
The crowned stag became the sigil of House
Baratheon, and Storm's End their seat.

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:08.860
Argilac's daughter would even remain in her
home, though, as a lady instead of a princess.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:15.010
The Stormlands were now Aegon's, and as tribute,
Aegon demanded the swords of the men Orys

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:16.660
had defeated.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:21.829
For what purpose, Orys didn't know.

00:14:21.829 --> 00:14:28.370
Jaime Lannister: Aegon now ruled two of the
Seven Kingdoms, but he would no longer be

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:30.200
able to take the rest piecemeal.

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:35.720
For the first time in thousands of years,
the kings put aside their squabbles and joined

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:38.160
forces against a common enemy.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:42.390
My ancestor, King Loren of House Lannister,
was head of the wealthiest family in the Seven

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:43.759
Kingdoms.

00:14:43.759 --> 00:14:48.470
When King Loren joined his forces to Mern
of House Gardener, King of the Reach, they

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:55.260
had the mightiest army in history, a so-called
iron fist to break the would-be conqueror.

00:14:55.260 --> 00:15:00.760
But while an iron fist can smash a man's face
in battle, you'd look silly hunting birds

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:05.330
or beasts with it, and Aegon had a creature
that was both.

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:09.329
The kings had never even seen a dragon, let
alone fought one.

00:15:09.329 --> 00:15:13.800
They had fought each other for thousands of
years, and victory always went to the larger

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.149
army.

00:15:15.149 --> 00:15:19.660
Surely a force five times that of Aegon's
could manage one dragon.

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:23.620
But Aegon arrived with three.

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:27.339
Still, the Lannisters and Gardeners hoped
for victory.

00:15:27.339 --> 00:15:31.310
The battlefield they chose was a wide plain
with firm ground and clear skies.

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:33.990
Perfect for archers and mounted cavalry.

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:38.589
But neither of the kings spared a thought
for why the ground was firm.

00:15:38.589 --> 00:15:44.329
There had been no rain for a fortnight, which
meant all the wheat and grass on it were bone-dry.

00:15:44.329 --> 00:15:46.029
Perfect for dragons.

00:15:46.029 --> 00:15:49.590
At first, the kings looked like they would
emerge victorious.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:54.210
When the horn blew for battle, their armies
swept around Aegon's flanks, and their iron

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:58.150
fist of mounted knights smashed through his
center before the dragons could even enter

00:15:58.150 --> 00:15:59.250
the fray.

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:04.930
But then Aegon and his sisters took flight
and unleashed their dragons, not on the soldiers,

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:08.139
but on the dry fields all around them.

00:16:08.139 --> 00:16:14.839
The iron fist unclenched and became a hand
outstretched for mercy.

00:16:14.839 --> 00:16:17.690
As Aegon promised, he had none.

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:22.589
More than four thousand men died in the fires,
another thousand escaping them.

00:16:22.589 --> 00:16:27.660
Tens of thousands returned home as monsters,
burned and scarred beyond recognition.

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:30.100
House Gardener never returned at all.

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:35.240
The Field of Fire, as the singers call it,
claimed the last of the Gardener line, and

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:40.220
House Tyrell rose in their stead as Lords
of the Reach and Wardens of the South.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:45.480
As for my illustrious ancestor, when King
Loren saw the battle was lost, he rode through

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:47.060
a wall of flame and smoke to safety.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:54.420
Or at least to a heroic capture a day later,
where he lay his sword before Aegon and knelt.

00:16:54.420 --> 00:17:00.040
Aegon, true to his word, spared him and confirmed
House Lannister as Lords of Casterly Rock

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:01.829
and Wardens of the West.

00:17:01.829 --> 00:17:02.829
Why wouldn't he?

00:17:02.829 --> 00:17:09.350
A Lannister always pays his debts, and now
we owed our lives to the crown.

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:13.360
That was worth centuries of subservience,
at least.

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:17.350
Besides, Aegon had a fetish for collecting
swords, not heads.

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:22.329
He added Loren's to the pile his men had retrieved
from the Field of Fire and sent them back

00:17:22.329 --> 00:17:23.620
to the Aegonfort.

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:33.049
Sansa Stark: With most of the South in Aegon's
hands, the best chance to throw back the Conqueror

00:17:33.049 --> 00:17:37.580
now lay with the North, if we cared enough
to try.

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:41.660
Unlike our southern rivals, the Stark Kings
of Winter didn't forge the North into one

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:48.230
kingdom for glory or gold (there is little
of either here), but to survive.

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:54.409
Alone in Westeros, the North remembered when
worse than dragons lay waste to armies.

00:17:54.409 --> 00:17:59.590
Thousands of years ago, the sun set on the
realms of men, and the Long Night began.

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:03.549
A new race emerged from the ice and snow:
the White Walkers.

00:18:03.549 --> 00:18:09.380
They demanded no crown, offered no terms,
spared no life, and the dead marched with

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:10.380
them.

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:16.000
With humanity facing extinction, a Stark sought
out the Children of the Forest, the most ancient

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:20.850
beings in Westeros, and convinced them to
ally with the men they'd once fought.

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:26.530
Together, the two races pushed the Walkers
back into the Land of Always Winter and sealed

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:32.919
it off from the Seven Kingdoms with the Wall,
three hundred miles of ice, stone, and earth

00:18:32.919 --> 00:18:35.080
rising nearly seven hundred feet tall.

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:40.730
To guard it, they established the Night's
Watch, a brotherhood sworn to defend the living

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:44.490
from the dead, whose vows erase both titles
and crimes.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:50.300
Viserys Targaryen: After the Long Night, the
North tried to forget it belonged to a continent.

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:53.400
Perhaps through pride, perhaps through sheer
ignorance.

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:56.350
You never can tell with the North.

00:18:56.350 --> 00:19:02.690
But as news of Aegon's dragons spread, Torrhen
Stark, the King of Winter, knew he couldn't

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:08.220
forget Westeros any longer and summoned his
lords to Winterfell.

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:13.230
Many fools shrugged off the threat while the
rest placed wages on how long the South would

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:14.650
take to burn.

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:20.700
Torrhen silenced them with a command to assemble
their armies and descend from the North in

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:21.700
force.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:26.820
Sansa: As the kings of the Rock and the Reach
burned on the Field of Fire, the greatest

00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:30.860
Northern force since the Long Night crossed
the Neck into the Riverlands.

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:36.909
But when King Torrhen arrived at the Trident,
he saw on the opposing riverbank the combined

00:19:36.909 --> 00:19:39.910
strength of all Aegon's conquered kingdoms.

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:46.070
A force larger than Torrhen's own by half,
and with three dragons.

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:51.799
Viserys: That night, King Torrhen called a
conference of all his lords and advisors.

00:19:51.799 --> 00:19:58.630
Some wanted to fight and trust Northern valor
to carry the day (and burn on the Trident).

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:03.860
The wisest of them wanted to withdraw to Moat
Cailin, the fortress which had thrown back

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:07.740
every southern invasion (and burn there).

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:14.340
One suicidal lord even wanted to ambush Aegon's
camp in the dark and kill the dragons as they

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:17.409
slept or at the very least, their riders.

00:20:17.409 --> 00:20:21.020
Hard to tell what would have been his fate.

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:22.070
Burning?

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:23.110
Beheading?

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:26.250
Dismemberment?Perhaps all three.

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:31.570
Sansa: My ancestor listened to their counsel,
and, in the morning, crossed the Trident under

00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:33.460
a flag of parley.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:38.659
Then King Torrhen of House Stark laid his
ancient crown at Aegon's feet and was named

00:20:38.659 --> 00:20:42.170
Lord of Winterfell and Warden of the North.

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:44.690
Viserys: And the King Who Knelt.

00:20:44.690 --> 00:20:50.039
Sansa: He had no choice, and thanks to him,
our soldiers returned to their homes whole

00:20:50.039 --> 00:20:52.010
and unharmed.

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:55.480
The swords that Aegon took from them were
not twisted, burnt, or mangled.

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:56.480
Viserys: Yet.

00:20:56.480 --> 00:21:04.710
Petyr Baelish: The Vale of Arryn was the last
of the great kingdoms left.

00:21:04.710 --> 00:21:11.090
Old and proud, House Arryn did what they always
did in times of strife: they shut the Bloody

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:13.640
Gate, sealing off the Vale.

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:19.990
Then, the Queen Regent Sharra of House Arryn
retreated with her son, the boy-king Ronnel,

00:21:19.990 --> 00:21:24.200
into the Eyrie, their family's impregnable
fortress.

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:29.460
From the top of their mountain, they could
look down on Westeros far below, its problems

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:31.810
hidden beneath the clouds.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:36.640
But one day, Queen Sharra entered the outer
courtyard to find her young son sitting on

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:41.590
the knee of Visenya Targaryen and ogling her
dragon, Vhagar, beside her.

00:21:41.590 --> 00:21:46.820
Just as he asked for another cake at dinner,
little King Ronnel asked his mother if he

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:49.870
could ride on the nice lady's dragon.

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:52.279
Visenya smiled at Sharra.

00:21:52.279 --> 00:21:56.909
So, Sharra imagined, did Vhagar.

00:21:56.909 --> 00:22:01.789
Remembering her manners, Sharra asked if she
could have Visenya brought some wine or food,

00:22:01.789 --> 00:22:05.130
she must be tired after such a long flight.

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:07.539
But Visenya demurred.

00:22:07.539 --> 00:22:11.980
Bored with his mother's pleasantries, Ronnel
demanded an answer.

00:22:11.980 --> 00:22:13.330
Poor boy.

00:22:13.330 --> 00:22:16.610
He didn't even understand the question.

00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:23.040
Sharra hesitated for a moment, then asked
Visenya, as a mother, if it was safe for the

00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:24.040
boy.

00:22:24.040 --> 00:22:26.670
Visenya assured her it was.

00:22:26.670 --> 00:22:28.950
What choice did Sharra have?

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:35.470
Whilst her son circled the castle, she collected
his little ringlet, her own regent's coronet,

00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:40.460
and the ancient Falcon Crown of Mountain and
Vale, which the Arryns had worn for thousands

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:42.390
of years.

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:47.470
Ronnel had taken to the sky as a king, but
he landed as a lordling.

00:22:47.470 --> 00:22:51.750
Perhaps he considered his ancient rights a
fair trade for a few minutes of flight, as

00:22:51.750 --> 00:22:53.900
a little boy would.

00:22:53.900 --> 00:23:00.200
More likely, he didn't even notice the three
crowns at Visenya's feet or recognize the

00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:03.900
swords of his garrison beside them.

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:13.450
Viserys Targaryen: The heads of Westeros had
bowed to Aegon, but its heart still beat free.

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:17.730
Oldtown, the center of the Faith of the Seven.

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:23.110
There dwelt the High Septon, the father of
the faithful, who commanded the obedience

00:23:23.110 --> 00:23:29.059
of all Westeros, save the savages of the North
and their Old Gods.

00:23:29.059 --> 00:23:34.250
When Aegon had landed in Westeros, the High
Septon had locked himself in the Starry Sept

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:39.789
and fasted for seven days and seven nights,
one for each of his gods.

00:23:39.789 --> 00:23:45.669
All he received for his trouble was the divine
wisdom that if Oldtown took up arms against

00:23:45.669 --> 00:23:51.610
the dragon, the city would burn, faithful
and faithless alike.

00:23:51.610 --> 00:23:57.010
After the submission of House Stark, Aegon
marches towards Oldtown, steeling himself

00:23:57.010 --> 00:23:59.030
for another battle.

00:23:59.030 --> 00:24:04.020
But he found the gates open, with the High
Septon welcoming him.

00:24:04.020 --> 00:24:09.770
The pious fool even had the arrogance to grant
what Aegon had already won, and anointed the

00:24:09.770 --> 00:24:16.539
last Valyrian as "Aegon of House Targaryen,
First of His Name, King of the Andals and

00:24:16.539 --> 00:24:21.899
the First Men, Lord of the Seven Kingdoms
and Protector of the Realm."

00:24:21.899 --> 00:24:27.470
As if titles meant anything to a man to whom
time itself now bowed.

00:24:27.470 --> 00:24:34.929
The maesters would hence divide all history
into Before and After Conquest.

00:24:34.929 --> 00:24:41.761
Most expected Aegon to stay and make Oldtown
his seat, but soon after his coronation, Aegon

00:24:41.761 --> 00:24:47.809
returned to the mouth of the Blackwater River,
where he had first set foot on Westeros.

00:24:47.809 --> 00:24:51.900
A small town had since sprouted around his
primitive fort.

00:24:51.900 --> 00:24:57.580
To honor their new master, the locals dubbed
it "King's Landing," though it looked more

00:24:57.580 --> 00:25:04.549
fit for a hedge knight, with wooden palisades,
muddy streets, and piles of mangled swords

00:25:04.549 --> 00:25:07.450
carted in from every corner of the conquest.

00:25:07.450 --> 00:25:14.409
But when Aegon made it his court, wood became
stone, black mud was buried beneath a Red

00:25:14.409 --> 00:25:20.770
Keep, and the collected swords of Aegon's
foes were blasted by dragon fire and became

00:25:20.770 --> 00:25:27.289
a seat fit for the Conqueror and the greatest
dynasty this world has ever known.

00:25:27.289 --> 00:25:32.780
House Targaryen.My family.My throne.

00:25:32.780 --> 00:25:38.340
Or so it should have been.

00:25:38.340 --> 00:25:45.570
Varys: But while Aegon titled himself Lord
of the Seven Kingdoms, in reality, he held

00:25:45.570 --> 00:25:47.150
only six.

00:25:47.150 --> 00:25:51.110
The seventh, Dorne, had never knelt.

00:25:51.110 --> 00:25:54.630
Visenya had flown into the Vale and returned
with its crown.

00:25:54.630 --> 00:26:00.419
Mimicking her sister, Rhaenys had flown over
the enemy force holding the passes into Dorne

00:26:00.419 --> 00:26:06.130
and landed in the castle of its ruling lady,
Princess Meria of House Martell.

00:26:06.130 --> 00:26:10.350
Meria was eighty years old, fat, bald, and
blind.

00:26:10.350 --> 00:26:15.340
Behind her back, many sniggered at her as
the "Yellow Toad of Dorne."

00:26:15.340 --> 00:26:18.299
The beautiful Rhaenys probably thought as
much when they met.

00:26:18.299 --> 00:26:23.130
She demanded Princess Meria kneel to her brother
Aegon, though she allowed that on account

00:26:23.130 --> 00:26:27.900
of Meria's age and health, a simple vow of
submission would do.

00:26:27.900 --> 00:26:33.130
But the princess told the queen that the Targaryens
weren't wanted in Dorne, and no Martell would

00:26:33.130 --> 00:26:36.980
ever bow, bend or break no matter how badly
they burned.

00:26:36.980 --> 00:26:42.280
Rhaenys could have mounted her dragon right
then, and roasted Meria in the castle as her

00:26:42.280 --> 00:26:44.320
brother had done at Harrenhal.

00:26:44.320 --> 00:26:50.150
But whatever she saw in Meria's eyes scared
her right back to King's Landing, with a dragon's

00:26:50.150 --> 00:26:53.010
tail between its legs.

00:26:53.010 --> 00:26:59.620
After Aegon's coronation, Rhaenys returned
to Dorne with Aegon and Visenya and their

00:26:59.620 --> 00:27:00.620
dragons.

00:27:00.620 --> 00:27:05.350
But no armies met them in the field, and no
lords defied them in their castles.

00:27:05.350 --> 00:27:09.870
As the dragons approached, Dorne simply emptied.

00:27:09.870 --> 00:27:13.909
House Martell had learned from Harrenhal and
the Field of Fire.

00:27:13.909 --> 00:27:18.760
The dragons were unbeatable in battle, but
wars were more than battles.

00:27:18.760 --> 00:27:21.860
Unopposed, Aegon claimed Dorne for his own.

00:27:21.860 --> 00:27:26.880
But as soon as he returned to King's Landing,
his castellans were hurled off towers, and

00:27:26.880 --> 00:27:31.010
his royal garrison vanished in the desert,
never to be seen again.

00:27:31.010 --> 00:27:38.279
Except, perhaps, when the winds change and
the sands cough up old bones and armor.Rhaenys

00:27:38.279 --> 00:27:43.690
returned on Meraxes, intent on avenging herself
against Meria Martell.

00:27:43.690 --> 00:27:46.080
But Dorne was no longer empty.

00:27:46.080 --> 00:27:52.190
The Dornish kept Meria's promise and fought
even while burning under dragon flame.

00:27:52.190 --> 00:27:54.669
And they won.

00:27:54.669 --> 00:27:59.809
One day a bolt pierced the eye of Meraxes
and knocked the dragon out of the sky.

00:27:59.809 --> 00:28:05.390
House Martell remained unbroken, unlike the
unfortunate Rhaenys.

00:28:05.390 --> 00:28:11.210
In their wrath, Aegon and Visenya set flame
to every castle and city but Sunspear, trying

00:28:11.210 --> 00:28:13.230
to turn the people against House Martell.

00:28:13.230 --> 00:28:19.630
But the Dornish stayed loyal, and when Aegon
returned to King's Landing, he found assassins

00:28:19.630 --> 00:28:22.610
waiting for him in the streets of his own
capital.

00:28:22.610 --> 00:28:27.880
If not for Visenya, the Conqueror would not
have enjoyed his conquest for very long.

00:28:27.880 --> 00:28:32.580
From then on, the king and his family would
be guarded by the seven greatest knights in

00:28:32.580 --> 00:28:36.029
the realm: the Kingsguard.

00:28:36.029 --> 00:28:40.909
When Meria died in her sleep, a weak and tired
son sued for peace.

00:28:40.909 --> 00:28:46.789
But old Meria had exhausted Aegon as well,
and he granted the request.

00:28:46.789 --> 00:28:51.309
The Targaryens still wanted Dorne, and eventually,
they would have it, but not at the point of

00:28:51.309 --> 00:28:52.490
a sword.

00:28:52.490 --> 00:28:57.159
They would buy it the same way great lords
buy anything: with a daughter.

